 "about": "T-170 #193/#200 (cap-finger-hero, 2026-10-10): v1 (the converter output of the user's C-146 part 1 touch log) has the user's 7 flings but not the stop taps: a touch that lands during momentum scrolling is not in the page's touch log (OBSERVED in our setup: the coast halts within one frame, e.g. 0.93 px/ms -> 0 at y 618, with no touchstart), so gesture-from-record never saw them. The user's scroll curve shows a stop after every up fling: +284 ms (y 618, then +20 px), +334 ms (y 781, then -41 px), +630 ms (y 766, then -28 px), +650 ms (y 779); the down flings coast back to the top unstopped. v2 adds a catch after each up fling. Limits of the robot: a stroke is >= 40 px (no pure tap), the next stroke starts ~0.85 s after a lift (WDA: ~0.25 s return + ~0.5-0.7 s start, runs 105127Z/105336Z), and a down stroke waits for a still page, so each catch is an up stroke of 40 px (press 80 ms, 120 ms move, 150 ms hold, no momentum) sent with no pause, landing ~0.85 s after the lift (the user: 0.28-0.65 s). To stop the page where the user's stopped (rest y 638, 740, 741, 779), each up fling's lift-off speed is fitted (coast = v x 0.478 s, measured in 105127Z s1; 84 % of it done at +0.87 s; lift-off = 1.79 x px/ms): ms 465 / 277 / 291 / 146 (compiled lift-off 941 / 1293 / 1263 / ~1540 px/s) for the user's px 236 / 199 / 206 / 137 (user ms 276 / 176 / 262 / 163). Down flings and their until y>=300 as in v1; pauses fitted so each down fling starts about when the user's did. Same input on both arms; fixed before any replay.",
